# Implementation workflow

- The canonical product documents are `docs/Game_design.md`, `docs/Content_design.md`, and `docs/implementation/`.
- Before implementing an IP module, follow `docs/implementation/WORKFLOW.md`.
- `docs/implementation/STATUS.md` is the only source of execution status.
- If the user requests the next module, select the first numerically ordered module with status `Ready`.
- Read the selected IP specification and its declared design context before editing code.
- Draft content is a non-binding compatibility target and cannot become production content without explicit approval.
- Run the module checks and update status/evidence/documentation impact in the same change.
- Route system changes to Game Design, entity/parameter changes to Content Design, and scope/dependency changes to the IP specification.
- Record cross-layer decisions in `docs/decisions/`; never treat a workaround as a product decision automatically.
